.TH jenkins-cli "1" "August 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Server Command"
.SH NAME
jenkins-cli \- Run Jenkins CLI commands against the configured controller
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jenkins-cli
.RI JENKINS_COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS\| .\|.\|.]
.br
.B jenkins-cli
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR HOST ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RI JENKINS_COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS\| .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B jenkins-cli
is a thin wrapper around
.BR jenkins-cli.jar .
It automatically determines the Jenkins controller URL from environment
variables or built-in defaults so that the user does not need to supply
.B \-s
.I URL
on every invocation.
.PP
All Jenkins CLI commands and their arguments are passed directly and
unchanged to
.BR jenkins-cli.jar .
The wrapper does not interpret, validate, or restrict Jenkins CLI commands.
New Jenkins CLI commands work without any changes to this wrapper.
.PP
The JAR is located via
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
so renaming the installation provider requires no changes to this script.
.PP
JVM options may be supplied via the
.SM JAVA_OPTS
environment variable.
.SH OPTIONS
The following options are consumed by the wrapper and not passed to Jenkins:
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
Controller host.
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_HOST
and the built-in default.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Controller port.
Overrides
.SM SMI_JENKINS_PORT
and the built-in default.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.PP
All other arguments are passed unchanged to
.BR jenkins-cli.jar .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_HOST
Controller host.
Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B SMI_JENKINS_PORT
Controller port.
Default:
.BR 7171 .
.TP
.B JAVA_OPTS
Additional JVM options.
.SH PRECEDENCE
.PP
.B --host
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_HOST
> 127.0.0.1
.PP
.B --port
>
.SM SMI_JENKINS_PORT
> 7171
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
List all jobs on the default controller:
.RS
.B jenkins-cli list-jobs
.RE
.PP
Trigger a build:
.RS
.B jenkins-cli build my-job
.RE
.PP
Trigger a build and wait for completion:
.RS
.B jenkins-cli build my-job -s
.RE
.PP
Get a job configuration:
.RS
.B jenkins-cli get-job my-job
.RE
.PP
Connect to a non-default controller:
.RS
.B jenkins-cli --host 192.168.1.10 --port 8080 list-jobs
.RE
.PP
Use environment variables for the controller address:
.RS
.nf
SMI_JENKINS_HOST=192.168.1.10
SMI_JENKINS_PORT=8080
.fi
.RS
.B jenkins-cli list-jobs
.RE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-jenkins-controller (1),
.BR smi-jenkins-node (1),
.BR smi-lib-location (1)
